LOGIN-FR-03 – Login and create account mods 
The Login page must support two form states 

Login Mode 

Create Account Mode 

The user must be able to switch between the two modes using the appropriate Login/create account control 

Acceptance Criteria: 

Login mode must display only the fields required for login.  

Create Account mode must display all fields required for account creation.  

Switching between modes must not cause errors or break the form. 

Page must initiate on the login mode 

 

LOGIN-FR-04 – Navigation After Login 
Following a successful login, the user should be able to access the team page 

Acceptance Criteria: 

A successful login must allow the user to access the Teams page. 

 

TEAMS-FR-01 – Team Name 
Team name must be visible on the teams' page 

Acceptance Criteria: 

Must not be empty 

Maximum of 25 Characters 

Must be visible on the Teams Page 

 

TEAMS-FR-02 – Member Name 
The name of each member shall be displayed below their profile portrait with the corresponding person 

Acceptance Criteria: 

Must not be empty 

Maximum of 30 Characters 

Long names must not overflow or break the page 

 

 

 

 

TEAMS-FR-03 – Member Photo 
A portrait of each member shall be displayed on the Teams page with the corresponding person 

Acceptance Criteria: 

Must use an accepted image format [JPG / PNG / WebP] 

Display Rules: 

Must be displayed above member name 

Must not appear stretched or distorted 

If image cannot be loaded, a fallback must be displayed 

 

TEAMS-FR-04 – Role 
Each Team member’s role shall be displayed with the corresponding person 

Acceptance Criteria: 

Must not be empty 

Maximum of 25 Characters 

 

TEAMS-FR-05 – Blurb 
A small blurb of the corresponding person shall be visible below their role 

Acceptance Criteria: 

A short blurb must be displayed for each team member 

Text must wrap correctly 

 Longer blurbs must not overlap other page content 

 

