5. Edge Cases 

5.1 Login Page 

 

LOGIN-EC-01 – Empty Login Fields 
Scenario: The user attempts to log in without entering an email or password. 

Expected Behaviour: 

Login must not proceed.  

Existing validation must inform the user that the required field is missing.  

The page must remain in Login mode. 

 

LOGIN-EC-02 – Invalid Login Credentials 
Scenario: The user enters an incorrect email or password. 

Expected Behaviour: 

The user must not be authenticated.  

Existing authentication error handling must be preserved.  

The user must remain on the Login page. 

 

LOGIN-EC-03 – Switching Between Login and Create Account Modes 
Scenario: The user repeatedly switches between Login and Create Account modes. 

Expected Behaviour: 

The form must continue to function correctly.  

Email and Password fields must remain visible.  

Name and Confirm Password fields must only appear in Create Account mode.  

Switching modes must not cause duplicate fields or page errors. 

 

LOGIN-EC-04 – Create Account With Missing Fields 
Scenario: The user attempts to create an account without completing all required fields. 

Expected Behaviour: 

Account creation must not proceed.  

Existing validation must identify the missing required fields.  

The form must remain in Create Account mode. 

 

LOGIN-EC-05 – Unsuccessful Login Navigation 
Scenario: The user's login attempt is unsuccessful. 

Expected Behaviour: 

The user must not be redirected to the Teams page.  

Access to the Teams page must only occur following successful authentication. 

 

5.2 Teams Page 

TEAMS-EC-01 – Missing Member Photo 
Scenario: A team member does not have a valid profile image. 

Expected Behaviour: 

A fallback/default image must be displayed.  

The member's Name, Role and Blurb must continue to display normally.  

The missing image must not break the page. 

 

TEAMS-EC-02 – Long Member Name 
Scenario: A member's name approaches the 30-character limit. 

Expected Behaviour: 

The name must remain readable.  

The text must not overflow its allocated area.  

The name must not overlap other content. 

 

TEAMS-EC-03 – Long Team Name 
Scenario: The team name approaches the maximum 25-character limit. 

Expected Behaviour: 

The team name must remain fully readable.  

It must not overflow or break the page layout. 

 

 

 

TEAMS-EC-04 – Long Role Name 
Scenario: A member's role approaches the maximum 25-character limit. 

Expected Behaviour: 

The role must remain readable.  

Text must wrap where necessary.  

The role must not overlap other content. 

 

TEAMS-EC-05 – Long Blurb 
Scenario: A team member has a significantly longer blurb than other members. 

Expected Behaviour: 

The text must wrap correctly.  

The blurb must not overlap the member's other information.  

The longer content must not break surrounding team member content. 

 

TEAMS-EC-06 – Multiple Team Members 
Scenario: The Teams page contains several team members with different name, role and blurb lengths. 

Expected Behaviour: 

Each member's information must remain associated with the correct person.  

One member's content must not overlap another member's content.  

All members must remain readable and identifiable. 

 
